      "Turn-flow example: 1. Players take turns asking the opponent for a specific rank (e.g. 8 or king). 2. The asker must hold at least one card of that rank. 3. If the opponent has cards of that rank, they give all of them to the asker. 4. If the opponent has none, the asker 'drinks': draw from the stock until finding a card of the requested rank. 5. Whenever a player has four of a kind, they discard it face up. 6. Winner is the first to empty their hand. If the stock runs out, the player with fewer cards wins. 7. Turns alternate regardless of whether the request was successful.",
